ccasionally have some  people from games media but it is  largely game development and then at the  end of the call you go on to vote on the  bafta website um and it's based on a  score so you can vote for your first  your second and your third and i think  you give them points if i remember  correctly but it's anonymous so you  actually don't know what everybody else  voted for so if somebody tried very hard  to convince you you still wouldn't  actually have to vote for whatever they  suggested indicate was pretty similar  except without the anonymity um and  for ndk they had discussions but i  couldn't join any of them because they  were at an exact point in time where i  have a meeting for my day job  every week but you get the nominees you  assign yourself to play a number of them  um and then for everyone else you kind  of explain what you thought of them so  the ndk jury very much has to trust each  other so i would write like a mini  review for everyone here's why i think  this um and then of the games that i was  like i really think this one should be  nominated for something i would also  read anybody else's reviews that are  extremely glowing about other things and  then made sure i played those games so  by the time we get to the nomination  point for each category  i have played the games that are  nominated um and we do the same thing  ranking by numbers but it's all publicly  listed and then somebody goes in  aggregates those and chooses which wins  in each category but you can outright  nominate something as well so it's a  very general consensus kind of thing so  yeah the game awards is the most  hands-off um i think ign the way they  did their internal one was also uh  google form which i believe anyone who  worked at the company could participate  in i don't imagine they let the sales  team participate in it  just something that i feel is really  worth noting is that the sales team  and the editorial team are very very  very separate i've seen people be like  oh it's a coincidence that  you know this game that gets this  advertising budget won this award  there is no way that any of the people  who are on the voting side at ign would  have any idea what sales deals are  coming up those teams do not talk they  are so separate they're not even allowed  to communicate ask to ask hey lana have  you played ac valhalla  i have not  um i've actually intentionally not not  played ac valhalla  because working at santa monica studio  obviously ragnarok is based in norse  mythology and i wanted to make the  active decision not to consume other  norse content i think someone at the  studio may have even suggested this to  me i don't remember  um but i didn't want to see other  examples of it so that nothing that i  thought would be influenced in any way  by it like i don't want to be influenced  in a way that's like oh this game's done  this though or in a way that's like oh  that's cool what if we did that so i  will not play ac valhalla actually um  while santa monica studio is actively  working on god of war ragnarok adam  prince said you have a question what is  the most underrated game in your opinion  and which would be the most overrated  i think i answered this my most recent q  a that i feel like the words underrated  and overrated  like are just very overused um so with  that context  a thing that i will admit that i don't  love those terms  it generally just means you like  something less or more than what you  think is the general consensus you know  i think that dragon's dogma is  criminally  underrated but even then it probably is  highly rated i just don't feel like it's  spoken about it's a 78 on metacritic so  it's not like it's really underrated  it's more than like i know i would rate  it higher than that i would totally rate  it higher than that i'd give it like a  nine it's more that i just feel like not  enough people talk about dragon's dogma  specifically darker risen was actually  the one that i preferred  in relation to how good i feel like that  game is i really love it and then the  most overrated i'm trying to think of  what's a game people really like that i  don't like that much i've never liked  the gameplay in bioshock a lot of great  things about both of those games all  three of them in fact but uh bioshock is  probably the most popular franchise that  while i have played all of them  i have never felt like i love any of  those games as much as a lot of other  people do there are things that i think  are brilliant about them but i don't  like  gush of the bioshock  like a lot of other people do and this  video is already really long so we're  gonna leave it there everybody  thank you all for watching remember that  you can find out more about keeps by  clicking the link in the description  below thank you again to them for  sponsoring these for such a long time i  appreciate it and i will see you guys  next time bye
 

